# Allowlist, not a denylist. Everything is excluded first and only the paths
# deploy/Dockerfile actually copies are added back, so a future `COPY . .` cannot bake
# deploy/.env — which holds FIBER_SECRETS_KEY, the database password and the admin
# password — into an image layer that anyone who can pull the image can read.
# Adding a COPY to deploy/Dockerfile means adding its source here too.
*

!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!crates

# Re-excluded from inside an allowed path: a per-crate build dir, editor droppings.
crates/**/target
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
